                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Alone in the Dark 3 is another fascinatingly weird entry, this time throwing its survival horror formula into a supernatural Old West setting. Haunted ghost towns, undead cowboys, and Edward Carnby somehow fit together remarkably well, and once again there’s a lot to admire about how imaginative these games were for their era. By this point the formula is familiar, though, and so are all of its rough edges. Awkward controls, cumbersome combat, and general compatibility-era jank can make actually playing it today considerably less fun than the ideas behind it. Still, taken as an early-’90s horror trilogy, Alone in the Dark 1–3 remains a really cool glimpse at developers figuring out a genre that would soon explode.",
